<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A small label that highlights a status, count, or category.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/badge)

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Badge(variant: :success) { "Active" }
```

Badge is a compact, non-interactive label for a piece of metadata - a status, a count, a tag, a
category. It renders a `<span>` and sizes to its content. Pick a `variant:` for the color scheme and
a `size:` for the scale; put an icon next to the text and tag it with `data: { icon: "start" }` /
`data: { icon: "end" }` so the padding tightens on that side.

To make a badge clickable (a filter chip, a category link), give it `href:` for an `<a>` or
`as: :button` for a `<button>`. It then becomes focusable and gains hover/press affordances.

## Examples

### Variants

Each variant carries a semantic color. The solid `primary`/`secondary` and tinted
`error`/`success`/`warning`/`info` schemes draw attention to a status, while `soft`, `outline` and
`primary_outline` stay quieter for neutral metadata.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :variants %>

```ruby
Badge(variant: :primary_outline) { "Primary outline" }
Badge(variant: :warning) { "Warning" }
```

### On dark backgrounds

The `light` variant is built for dark or photographic backgrounds - a translucent white fill that
reads against the surface beneath it.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :on_dark %>

### Sizes

Four sizes scale the badge from `:xs` to `:lg`. The text and any icons scale together.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :sizes %>

### With an icon

Place an icon before or after the text and tag it with `data: { icon: "start" }` or
`data: { icon: "end" }` - the badge tightens the padding on that edge so the icon sits snug.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :with_icon %>

```ruby
Badge(variant: :success) do
  svg(data: { icon: "start" }, ...) { |s| s.path(d: check_icon) }
  plain "Verified"
end
```

### Icon only

`size: :icon_sm`, `:icon_md` and `:icon_lg` render a square badge for a lone icon. Give it an
`aria_label:` so the meaning is announced.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :icon_only %>

```ruby
Badge(variant: :warning, size: :icon_lg, aria_label: "Boosted") { bolt_icon }
```

### Notification count

Absolutely position a small badge against an icon button to surface an unread count. Keep the
number in the badge and the full meaning in its `aria_label:`.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :notification_count %>

```ruby
div(class: "relative inline-flex") do
  Button(variant: :outline, icon: true, aria_label: "Notifications") { bell_icon }
  Badge(variant: :secondary, size: :xs, class: "absolute -inset-e-1.5 -top-1.5 min-w-4 px-1 font-medium",
        aria_label: "#{count} unread notifications") { count.to_s }
end
```

### Interactive (link or button)

`href:` turns the badge into a link, `as: :button` into a `<button>`. It becomes focusable and
animates on hover and press.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :interactive %>

```ruby
Badge(variant: :soft, href: tag_path(tag)) { tag.name }
Badge(variant: :primary_outline, as: :button, data: { action: "follow#toggle" }) { "Follow" }
```

### RTL

The icon flips to the start (right) edge and the tightened padding follows, because both are
expressed with logical properties.

<%= embed UI::BadgePreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Badge

Renders a `<span>`, or an `<a>` / `<button>` when interactive. Every other attribute is forwarded.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:primary`, `:primary_outline`, `:secondary`, `:soft`, `:outline`, `:error`, `:success`, `:warning`, `:info`, `:light` | `:primary` | Color scheme. |
| `size:` | `:xs`, `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg`, `:icon_sm`, `:icon_md`, `:icon_lg` | `:md` | Scale. The `icon_*` sizes render a square badge for a lone icon. |
| `href:` | `String` | - | Render an `<a>`; makes the badge focusable and interactive. |
| `as:` | `:span`, `:a`, `:button` | `:span` | The element to render; `:button` gets `type="button"`. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

The root carries `data-variant` and `data-size` (e.g. `primary-outline`, `icon-sm`) for styling hooks.

## Accessibility

- A plain Badge is a `<span>` - purely visual. Don't rely on color alone to convey meaning; back it
  with text (e.g. "Active", not just a green badge).
- For an icon-only badge, supply an `aria_label:` so the icon's meaning is announced.
- For a count badge, keep the visible number short and put the full meaning in `aria_label:`
  (e.g. "3 unread notifications").
- When you make a badge interactive, use `href:` or `as: :button` so it's a real `<a>` or `<button>`:
  keyboard-focusable and announced with the correct role.
- Hover/press transitions are skipped when the user prefers reduced motion.
